## Finite selectors

1. `--component-compare-left`: genuine old Challenge and fresh changed Challenge, each with J0/P0/S0/WEAPON-01. Each must obtain its first actual native tracking/armed cycle and execute the original proof through warning, lock, active and recovery, real escape/positioning dashes, exactly one ordinary primary and complete canonical cadence, unchanged Hero HP and positive target HP. Same completed fork landing must put old housing within ordinary reach and changed opposite housing outside it; both executed return/hit receipts must exist. This is a concrete changed approach requirement, not merely a different source ID/warning. If this distinction or native feasibility fails, no authored-decision credit follows.
2. `--component-short-slow-right`: changed Challenge only, J0/P2/S2/WEAPON-03. Same normal native response assertions; this is one representative combined short/slow sample, not an all-kit matrix or new baseline comparison.
3. `--component-portrait`: changed neutral left route obtains one genuine original armed lease, then pauses normally and captures one actual540×1170 view. It requires nonempty real Player/all-seven actor/Scheduler/Exchange packets plus actual input, camera/HUD optics and mesh/sprite render witnesses. Native `var_to_bytes` before/after draw must agree; the draft writes both original `.var` files, encoded Exact observations and PNG. Root must inspect actual pixels. This selector ends after the still and normal cleanup; it requires no graphical bot combat completion or green-photo replay. No later graphic response is claimed.

One selector per child, a fresh absolute `CINDER_A2_L1_COMPONENT_REPORT` pointing inside its Root phase, no reused output. Suggested owned child ceilings:180s for each headless selector,210s graphical. Limits bound the child, not gameplay timing. Draft syntax has not been checked by Godot and no future command is credited as executed:

```text
CINDER_A2_L1_COMPONENT_REPORT=/absolute/new-phase/native-report.exact.json
python3 scripts/dev/dev.py engine --headless --path . --script res://tests/act2_l1_arrangement_component.gd -- --component-compare-left
